id: pm-memory-1363
title: Preserve guidance validity in portable harness round trips
description: Define interoperable policy-window metadata and renewal history for portable harness files.
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T22:03:10.834Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T13:57:33.527Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Bounded guidance can round trip without becoming unbounded or silently losing evidence; imported windows are validated before writes.
parent: pm-memory-0kwy
comments[100]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T01:04:43.613Z",codex-agent,"Claimed portable policy-window work. Design inspection: existing transfer refuses bounded guidance and sequential imports can partially publish. Investigating SDK transactions and existing lease/history surfaces before selecting an atomic import contract. Will preserve window evidence and renewal ancestry, reject broadened or removed bounds, and validate in non-git trackers with crash and competing-writer boundaries."
  "2026-10-25T01:15:25.678Z",codex-agent,"Implemented versioned policy inventory plus editable body files, exact window and renewal validation, full-batch SDK preview/commit, deterministic recovery ids, foreign-record skips, and staged export publication. Targeted suite: 24 passed before the final update/rollback and independent-export tests were added. Randomized sets cover both harnesses, mixed bounded/unbounded guidance, kinds, tags and renewal counts. Existing unbounded byte-preserving transfers remain supported. CI now invokes the explicit npm release:check gate as well as the existing Bun gate; local full release gates are intentionally deferred to CI on this saturated host."
  "2026-10-25T01:17:54.916Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public-copy validation passed: 17 public items, 6 nonempty bodies, 232693 projected input bytes; 17 derived scenario guidance records, 34 renewal records retained per harness, 19 exported files per harness, all 17 unchanged on identical retries, zero lost windows/evidence, edited bodies needs-renewal. Every source file was permission-protected and its aggregate fingerprint remained unchanged. Evidence: docs/portable-guidance-validation.md. The first unrestricted read created only SDK runtime metadata caches, so the measured run used an independently extracted read-only copy."
  "2026-10-25T01:21:28.721Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: in an isolated source snapshot with only transfer.ts restored from origin/main, node --test test/portable.test.ts failed all 16 new regressions (0 pass, 16 fail). Additional focused behavioral reversions preserved the new exporter: restoring only legacy importDir failed 5/5 selected import/refusal/atomic/concurrency regressions; replacing deterministic import ids with random ids failed the SDK crash-recovery regression; removing the writer lease failed the competing-import peer-success regression. Production sources were never reverted in place. Current targeted portable suite: 16/16 pass, with src/portable.ts measured at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks pass. The pm-linked npm run typecheck passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress."
  "2026-10-25T01:21:30.096Z",codex-agent,"SDK usage: certified listAllComplete, native get/history verification, settings/schema APIs, acquireLockLease/fence, previewItemMutations, commitItemMutations, resolveAuthorIdentity and host TOON/JSON rendering. SDK limitation: PmClient has no bound batch-commit method; the public commitItemMutations helper requires an explicit filesystem pmRoot, so hosted backend acceptance is not claimed. Its atomicity is logical with compensation/recovery; unrelated readers and writers outside the package lease are not isolated. No SDK core behavior was reimplemented."
  "2026-10-25T01:24:34.632Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/15 . Final ownership review added filtering before memory decoding: unrecognized-source Knowledge records, including malformed foreign metadata, are skipped with explicit reasons and never adopted or deleted. Focused current tests: 5/5 pass. Removing only the ownership-filtered read makes the new malformed-foreign-record regression fail. The initial CI is running explicit npm release gates on Node 22/26 and Bun on Node 26."
  "2026-10-25T01:27:02.571Z",codex-agent,"Initial Node 26 CI release gate ran 262 tests with 262 pass and zero skips, then correctly refused 99.9% branch coverage (100% required): transfer.ts had a platform-specific rename-code branch. Replaced the equivalent code comparison with a platform-independent recognized-code set and added a real filesystem permission failure/retry regression. Thresholds remain unchanged. Local pm health reports only managed extension host skew (pinned SDK 2026.10.23 versus the local pm-github build 2026.10.24); history integrity is clean and CI tracker health passed. No dependency pin or shared extension configuration was changed."
  "2026-10-25T01:28:04.418Z",codex-agent,"Final fixture correction uses the SDK create options object; npm run typecheck and the malformed-foreign-record regression now pass. The real publication-permission regression also passes, and restoring only the original publish function makes it fail (missing expected refusal). Source implementation is ready for orchestrator review in PR 15; the item stays in_progress. Claim is released while the final unchanged-threshold npm/Bun CI gates verify the pushed revision; exact run URLs and counts are maintained in the PR evidence."
  "2026-10-25T02:45:48.043Z",codex-agent,"Review reopened the class of stateful round-trip defects: content-addressed replay can suppress A/B/A updates, raw provenance is not SDK-normalized, and policy transfers drop native relationships. Reclaimed the existing item. Will bind replay identity to target history, use SDK write/read normalization as the provenance oracle, preserve typed relationships, and replace the narrow property with at least 500 seeded state-machine sequences read back through the SDK after every operation."
  "2026-10-25T03:11:14.421Z",codex-agent,"Three focused regressions now pass: A/B/A updates read back as A; newline/CRLF imports retry without false native-edit skips; mixed bounded/unbounded graph edges retain kinds and targets, including removals. Revert proofs in isolated snapshots: content-only transaction identity fails older-manifest replay (0 pass/1 fail); raw-body provenance comparison fails whitespace retries (0/1); removing exported relationships fails the mixed graph round trip (0/1). The normalized baseline is captured from SDK reads after writes and committed in a second recoverable batch. Target history anchors plus the frozen pending plan cover both stages; expanded create/update crash tests pass (14 SDK transitions for two records). The 500-sequence model is running."
  "2026-10-25T03:13:23.140Z",codex-agent,"The review model has passed more than 380 independent sequences so far without a failure. It compares complete semantic content, bounds, and relationship targets/kinds against a reference model after every step, using raw SDK-read normalized snapshots only as the provenance oracle. Expanded boundary testing passes: both SDK data and provenance transactions recover from every create/update transition; foreign or corrupt pending records are skipped or refused without adoption. Targeted coverage measured portable-plan.ts at 100% in all four dimensions. Portable relationship metadata is now required in the Memory SDK projection, preventing callers from accidentally representing a native graph only as an untyped id list."
  "2026-10-25T03:17:25.138Z",codex-agent,"Model property PASS: 500 independent seeded sequences, 7500 complete SDK-read state comparisons, master seed 0x1363cafe (325307134), per-sequence seed = (master + imul(index, 0x9e3779b9)) >>> 0. Operations: export, import archived/older manifests with A/B/A, native body/description/relationship edits, leading/trailing whitespace and CRLF variants, link additions/removals, mixed bounded/unbounded guidance, final native rebase and import(X)==X. Zero failures, skips or cancellations. Each failure prints master seed, sequence seed, operation and step. Three targeted review regressions pass; targeted crash/compensation tests pass; four pending-plan/relationship validation tests pass. Source typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero duplication pass. SDK gaps retained: PmClient has no bound batch helper; previewItemMutations does not expose normalized staged values, so provenance uses actual SDK write/read capture; no public journal-status reader is exposed, so the owned SDK snapshot journal is inspected read-only for completion. Native SDK edge import reasserts author_source; kinds, targets, author/time/source data and original input remain retained."
  "2026-10-25T04:11:33.436Z",codex-agent,"CI c6a1567: npm and Bun on Node 26 each passed 272 tests, 2 packed acceptance tests, 500 sequences/7500 state checks and 100% coverage across 28 sources. Node 22 passed its other 271 tests but hit the 30-minute model-test timeout after 100 sequences (no assertion failure). Clock-only profiling showed no meaningful improvement. Optimized the harness instead: one certified SDK read now supplies both independent model checks and normalized provenance, and each case clones a verified initial A state INCLUDING completed journals instead of redundantly recreating it. Every case still performs A/B/A, six random operations, final rebase, and 15 SDK-read checks; all 500 sequences and 7500 checks are retained. Per-sequence subtests bound test-runner resources and expose seeds individually; the full-case time allowance is 90 minutes. Production fixes and coverage thresholds are unchanged. Local Node 22 coverage profile passes all 10 sampled sequences/150 checks. The unchanged full 500-sequence optimized run is active locally."
  "2026-10-25T04:16:49.717Z",codex-agent,"Harness optimization retains the full reference model, operation alphabet, seed formula and 7500 sequence-step SDK assertions. It seeds and verifies A/B/A once via SDK, copies the completed A journals into each independent tracker, then tests the exact A retry, B update and older A replay in every sequence. Each step performs one complete SDK read shared by content/graph assertions and the read-back provenance oracle; native snapshots are accepted as baselines only after content/graph equality passes. Each sequence has its own subtest and fail-fast completion assertion. The default count remains 500, with six random operations plus the fixed replay/rebase steps. No SDK mocks, skip paths or reduced coverage thresholds were added. Typecheck, lint and zero duplication pass after the optimization."
  "2026-10-25T05:50:52.899Z",codex-agent,"Final candidate CI confirms npm and Bun on Node 26: 772 tests plus 2 packed acceptance tests per gate, all 500 sequences/7500 checks, 28 sources at 100% in every dimension. Node 22 hit the 90-minute parent timeout after 239 completed sequence subtests (510 total passing tests, zero assertion failures). Its per-sequence time grows from about 3 seconds to 40-59 seconds. Will bound process lifetime to ten independent sequences per real Node worker while retaining the identical 500 global seeds, operations, SDK assertions and coverage collection. No production changes or coverage exclusions are planned."
  "2026-10-25T05:53:10.181Z",codex-agent,"The new worker model still detects each behavioral revert in isolated snapshots: content-only identity fails master/sequence seed 325307134 at sequence 0 step 6 (older A replay); raw-body provenance fails the SDK-verified seed B application; omitted relationships fail the seed graph import. Every mutant exits nonzero. Parent orchestration also refuses a worker that exits zero without a complete SDK-read receipt. The existing testEnvironment helper clears inherited Node test-runner context while retaining NODE_V8_COVERAGE for real child-process source coverage."
  "2026-10-25T05:55:42.412Z",codex-agent,"Worker lifetime validation PASS under real Node 22 c8: two consecutive ten-sequence workers completed all 20 sequences/300 SDK-read checks, parent 3/3 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips. Worker durations 52.5 and 43.7 seconds; production source coverage was collected from the children. The first single-process 90-minute run remains a failed gate, not accepted evidence. Full CI now runs 50 workers with exactly the same 500 global seeds and 7500 checks; no source behavior or thresholds changed. Current typecheck, lint and docstrings pass. Temporary profile sources are removed before duplication and commit."
  "2026-10-25T07:40:06.627Z",codex-agent,"Round-two review retains the round-trip fixes but identifies moved-state defects: recovery overwrites edits made after intent, skipped foreign targets leave dependent edges, and saved-input equality can misreport current content. Reclaimed the existing item. Will use SDK revision compare-and-set on every mutation, close plans under skipped dependencies, compare unchanged against current SDK state, and extend the same 500 seeded model with recovery/native-edit/ownership/body-restoration transitions plus behavioral revert proofs."
  "2026-10-25T08:13:36.655Z",codex-agent,"Implemented target revision/history expectations, SDK item-lock CAS via BulkItemUpdateMutation.match on updated_at, unique-key guards for creations, and revision guards before replay and at SDK boundaries. A moved plan interrupts SDK forward replay without compensating over the newer edit, then returns a typed conflict; conflicting intents stay preserved for explicit reconciliation. Snapshot batches are now frozen too. Skip roots close transitively over dependent rows before mutation selection. Unchanged compares current SDK content with incoming values through canonicalDocument and itemDocumentToMutationOptions, not saved input. The original 18 portable regressions and all six review regressions pass, including native edits at every journal boundary and fresh CAS boundaries. Expanded model retains 500 seeds, now 33 checks per sequence (16500 total); sampled eight sequences passed before the local timer, with no assertion failure. Five-sequence workers bound instrumentation state; full gates remain CI-only."
  "2026-10-25T08:31:08.944Z",codex-agent,"Closed the related partially-created graph case by staging all new nodes without edges via an SDK transaction, then reading their real revisions before the CAS data/relationship batch. Node/data/provenance stages retain frozen recovery payloads; a native edit between stages refuses before overwrite, and a foreign target appearing after the first node cannot leave a dangling edge. Tests now inject every one of the 21 SDK boundaries for two-record creations and all 15 for a one-record competing import, plus package stage boundaries. Explicit moved-state conflicts preserve the intent; the remedy names only the owned intent for preservation/removal after review and asks for a reviewed current export. No foreign records or SDK journals are deleted."
  "2026-10-25T08:33:15.552Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs PASS in isolated source snapshots, with production never reverted in place. Removing revision/history guards and SDK CAS matches fails the focused newer-edit recovery regression and model sequence 0 step 32 (retry preserves newer native edit). Removing skip closure fails the focused foreign graph/retry regression and model sequence 0 step 28 (skip closure stays retryable). Restoring saved-input unchanged detection fails the focused native-A restore/retry-B regression and model sequence 0 step 19 (retry restore B). All model counterexamples print MASTER_SEED=325307134 and SEQUENCE_SEED=325307134. Each focused mutant has 0 pass/1 fail; each model mutant has 0 pass/2 fail including the fail-fast parent. Current five-sequence worker passes 6/6 tests and all 165 SDK-read checks, zero failures/cancellations/skips."
  "2026-10-25T10:05:46.536Z",codex-agent,"Model extended further to include 100 fresh-tracker branches within the same 500 sequences: all node/data/provenance journal boundaries, plus foreign ownership after a creation crash. The model now enforces 16933 SDK-read state checks, including no dangling references and stable repeated recovery. Samples at sequence starts 0 and 50 pass 12/12 tests, 10 sequences and 339 state checks. The SDK delete-compensation path reserves deleted IDs (item_identity_reserved); node recovery allocates fresh IDs and remaps edges through SDK converters while retaining the old history. All 12 node/data/provenance compensation boundaries converge; mixed existing/new graph tests and native-peer-before-rollback tests pass. Intent writes and removals are lease-fenced and compare the last owned token, preserving a foreign replacement instead of overwriting/deleting it."
  "2026-10-25T10:19:20.920Z",codex-agent,"Ready for full CI: targeted portable/plan/review suite 38/38 passed, no failures/cancellations/skips. c8 measured portable.ts, portable-plan.ts and portable-replan.ts at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero duplication pass. Intent replacement/removal now compares an operation-bound token under the live lease, retains late foreign/corrupt/amended files, and recognizes a peer-drained completed intent as success. SDK-owned partial progress matching the current input can capture its baseline without falsely claiming a native edit. The three reviewed behavioral reverts fail both focused and seeded model regressions, recorded above. Full 500-sequence/16933-check model and complete npm/Bun release gates are deferred to CI on the pushed head; final run URL and counts will be maintained in PR 15. SDK gap found and handled: delete compensation reserves IDs in history (item_identity_reserved), so node recovery rebinds identities and relationships rather than reusing a reserved identity."
  "2026-10-25T14:10:08.619Z",codex-agent,"Round-three review reproduced transaction identity reuse after deletion, a compensated-recovery read/guard race, partial writes on mid-batch revision refusal, and canceled-link export failure. Reclaimed the item. Will use per-attempt journal identities, one shared revision-read/guard/CAS helper, SDK compensation for moved-state refusals with retryable owned-intent cleanup, and external-reference receipts for excluded targets. Extend fixed and 500-sequence model regressions, record behavioral revert proofs, and wait for exact-head npm/Bun CI gates."
  "2026-10-25T14:25:37.459Z",codex-agent,"Round-three implementation now assigns a fresh per-attempt UUID digest recorded by the intent, shares revision read/guard/CAS preparation across fresh and recovery paths, and uses ordinary SDK compensation for moved-state refusals. Added SDK beforeMutation guards under item locks to prevent compensation restoring over peer revisions, plus a recoverable SDK rollback transaction across stages before owned intent cleanup. Export omits canceled, missing and artifact targets with typed omitted_links receipts. Delete/re-import and external-link fixed regressions pass; checking serialized memory-document restoration separately from append-only audit history, which SDK compensation intentionally extends."
  "2026-10-25T14:54:34.933Z",codex-agent,"All four review reproductions now have real-tracker fixed cases. Shared read/guard/CAS boundary tests and serialized memory-document rollback/retry checks pass; the SDK lock-scoped compensation guard refuses to restore over a peer. Added crash injection at every SDK rollback transition, fresh-attempt collision checks against existing journal files, stale-completed-intent delete/re-import recovery, and transitive peer-reference preservation. The model retains 500 seeds and now enforces 22933 SDK-read checks, adding two delete/re-import generations, mid-batch refusal state equality, and every shared-helper boundary across fresh/interrupted/compensated paths. Typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero duplication pass. Behavioral revert snapshots are running; final targeted coverage and exact-head CI remain pending."
  "2026-10-25T14:56:42.596Z",codex-agent,"Round-three behavioral revert proofs passed in isolated source snapshots. Restoring live-item-only input/history transaction identity fails delete/re-import (focused 0 pass/1 fail; model 0 pass/2 fail, sequence 0 step 24 reimport recreated generation, seed 325307134). Restoring guard-before-read ordering fails a compensated recovery peer edit (focused 0/1; model 2 pass/2 fail including parent, sequence 2 step 28, seed 1339211376). Making PlanMoved an SDK interruption again fails mid-batch memory state equality (focused 0/1; model 0/2, sequence 0 step 25, seed 325307134). Master seed 0x1363cafe; every mutant exits nonzero for behavioral assertions, with no module or syntax failure. Production files were never reverted in place."
  "2026-10-25T15:04:25.849Z",codex-agent,"The model parent and linked command now allow four hours for the expanded remote coverage run. This adds time for two complete deletion/recreation generations and guarded rollback in every sequence; all 500 seeds, 22933 SDK-read assertions, 100 fresh-tracker branches and 100 percent coverage thresholds remain mandatory. Five-sequence workers retain the existing bounded instrumentation lifetime. No local full release gate is being run on the saturated host."
  "2026-10-25T17:09:28.825Z",codex-agent,"Additional targeted results: the initial 55-test portable suite passed, the latest 15 rollback tests passed, and foreign export/wrong-type identity refusal passed after correcting a test fixture to look up the SDK-created item through the complete SDK list. Final local coverage is running against frozen production files. Import and export now filter foreign ownership and decode content from one certified SDK snapshot, including wrong-type memory identities. Allocation delegates hashing to SDK deriveMutationTransactionId with a UUID persisted in the intent. Model samples at starts 0, 50, 150 and 200 passed 20 sequences/919 SDK-read checks; the node-commit-before-readback refusal is distinguished from an accepted fresh retry. Full 500-sequence gates remain CI-only."
  "2026-10-25T17:22:50.684Z",codex-agent,"Round-three validation: the four targeted portable suites passed 58/58, and the final foreign-intent recovery case passed separately, giving 59 distinct passing regressions with zero failures/cancellations/skips. Combined c8 measurement covers portable.ts, portable-plan.ts, portable-replan.ts and portable-rollback.ts at 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. Typecheck, lint and docstring gates pass; shared test helpers retain the unchanged zero-duplication threshold. Four sampled five-sequence workers pass all 20 sequences and 919 SDK-read checks. Full 500-sequence/22933-check model and npm/Bun release gates will run on the pushed head in CI; final run receipts will be maintained in PR 15. The original read-only public-copy measurements remain unchanged. SDK gaps: PmClient has no bound batch commit; previewItemMutations exposes no normalized staged values; no public transaction-journal status/abort/replan reader; unconditional SDK bulk restoration requires item-lock mutation guards and a separate monotonic SDK rollback transaction; delete compensation reserves identities and requires SDK edge remapping. Refusal restores memory document bytes while the SDK audit remains append-only; newer peer revisions and adopted support graphs are retained. Hosted acceptance remains unverified."
  "2026-10-25T17:23:18.989Z",codex-agent,"Final three helper-refactored rollback regressions pass 3/3; duplication is 0%, typecheck/lint/docstrings pass (35 files, 140 documented declarations). Changelog generation and check pass. Local strict pm health retains one environment-only extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew: pinned host 2026.10.23 versus separately installed pm-github 2026.10.25. Tracker integrity and history_drift checks are OK. No dependency pins or external extensions were changed; clean CI health remains required. Claim released; item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-25T18:28:17.399Z",codex-agent,"First round-three CI candidate ae1b222 completed all 500 model sequences and 22933 SDK-read comparisons, with the full source table at 100% in all four dimensions. The Node 26 npm gate stopped at 405/406 tests because an older legacy-export regression asserted the exact two-field receipt and did not yet expect the new omitted_links contract. Updated that existing assertion to require the precise canceled and artifact receipts while retaining every emitted-file, byte-preservation and re-import assertion. node --test test/review-r10.test.ts passes 4/4; the pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress also passes. Typecheck, lint and zero duplication pass. No production source changed after ae1b222. A new exact-head CI run remains required; the failed and superseded run is not full-gate evidence."
  "2026-10-26T10:43:40.885Z",codex-agent,"Reopened the ownership class after native Task links were cleared by an unchanged bounded-guidance round trip. Will compute portable changes against the exported baseline, preserve absent/native-only fields and relationships, add independent SDK-read identity/locality/foreign-preservation laws with at least 500 sequences each, audit other import/sync entry points, and record a behavioral clearing revert proof. Existing recovery and prior round-trip evidence remain retained."
  "2026-10-26T10:51:53.357Z",codex-agent,"Ownership design: new exports carry immutable per-field baseline hashes and explicitly represented baseline relationships. Existing records receive selective three-way field/dependency patches, with omitted/native-only state preserved and no native bookkeeping rewrites. The existing SDK snapshot transaction will retain the portable ownership receipt outside native item fields, preserving older-manifest replay without adopting foreign edges. Existing SDK CAS/history guards and guarded compensation remain required; no manual ledger writer is added. Audit found importPolicy plus the legacy Claude/AGENTS/Cursor importDir path; command dispatch delegates to these, and the package has no separate sync entry point."
  "2026-10-26T11:26:00.754Z",codex-agent,"Ownership regression reproduced before the fix: unchanged bounded guidance linked to a native Task was reported updated and lost the edge. Behavioral revert proof in an isolated source copy: restore clearDeps/replaceDeps over only incoming portable relationships while keeping every other fix; the native-Task SDK-state regression fails (0 pass/1 fail), and independent identity law (a) fails at sequence 0, master/sequence seed 325300385, requested kind blocks, target class active-memory (0/1). The SDK diff shows omitted native/canceled/missing/artifact/foreign edges disappearing. Both failures are behavioral assertions, not syntax/module errors; production files were never reverted in place. Current samples pass 16 sequences per new law (48 total) and five retained stateful sequences/229 SDK-read checks. Full CI will run 500 sequences for EACH ownership law plus the existing 500-sequence recovery model."
  "2026-10-26T13:01:46.951Z",codex-agent,"Ownership audit: policy imports now use immutable SDK-normalized field/edge baselines and selective SDK additions/removals; omitted native Task, canceled, missing, artifact, foreign and other nonrepresented links are unknown, never deletion authority. Existing records retain native lifecycle, original-source bytes, paths, verification, recall and unknown metadata. Legacy claude-code, agents-md and cursor imports use the same ownership split and recoverable SDK batch; only explicitly present legacy fields and wiki additions grant authority. Generated legacy projections fall back to the policy format; genuinely lossless legacy files retain bytes. Native identity changes are recognized from immutable SDK creation history instead of mutable provenance. Fixed Task-link identity and adapter audits pass; independent locality sample (16 sequences) and existing stateful sample (5 sequences, 229 SDK-read checks) pass. Full ownership laws remain 500 per law in CI."
  "2026-10-26T13:04:46.579Z",codex-agent,"Final clearing-only revert proof: copied the current implementation into an isolated non-git project and changed only ownershipPatch relationship mutation construction back to incoming-only clearDeps/replaceDeps. The production worktree was untouched. Focused Native Task source-round-trip regression: 0 passed, 1 failed; SDK read-back lost the Task edge. Independent identity law: 0 passed, 1 failed at MASTER_SEED=325300385, SEQUENCE=0, SEED=325300385; SDK read-back lost omitted native, canceled, artifact, missing and foreign-target edges. With the selective ownership fix, the fixed case and 16-sequence identity/locality/foreign samples pass; CI runs all 500 sequences per law."
  "2026-10-26T13:34:01.942Z",codex-agent,"Round-five validation: ownership regressions pass 16/16 through the pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress. Import/export adapter audit passes 55/55, plus the revised AGENTS policy round-trip case passes 1/1. The 59-test portable protocol run passed 54 tests; its five compatibility failures were stale tracker-local identity/provenance expectations and a copied fixture identity, all corrected and then passed in focused reruns (2+2+1). Ten existing stateful sequences pass 459 SDK-read checks (starts 0 and 50; master 0x1363cafe). Independent law samples pass 64 sequences: identity 32 (bounded and unbounded), locality 16 bounded plus 16 unbounded, foreign 16 unbounded; the separate law receipts record each exact count and seed. Typecheck/lint/docstrings pass, zero duplication and privacy/history-prefix checks pass. Full 500-per-law ownership execution plus the 500-sequence/22933-check state machine and npm/Bun release gates are deferred to exact-head CI on this saturated host. SDK gaps remain: no PmClient-bound batch API, previewItemMutations/previewItemMutationDocument return validation/warnings rather than normalized staged values, and no public transaction-journal read/abort/replan API. Use canonicalDocument plus SDK writes/read-back, owned journal reads, guarded SDK compensation and reserved-ID remapping. Public-copy measurements remain as documented; hosted acceptance is unverified."
  "2026-10-26T13:34:33.593Z",codex-agent,"Count correction: the ownership-law samples total 80 sequences, not 64: identity 32, locality 32, foreign preservation 16. Masters are 325300385, 342209445 and 359118505; each sequence seed is (master + imul(index, 0x9e3779b9)) >>> 0. The per-law counts in the preceding comment were correct. The additional legacy compensated-create regression validates reserved-ID replanning with raw harness provenance; its input is not misparsed as a policy manifest. Revert proofs and fixed review sequences from prior rounds remain in this item's append-only comments; the newest Task-link case and clearing-only law counterexample are recorded above. Final CI receipts will be attached to PR 15 without changing the tested head."
  "2026-10-26T14:43:18.174Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI candidate 9790fbd was not accepted: Node 26 passed all 500 retained model sequences/22933 SDK-read checks, but six tests failed. Three expected legacy generated filenames/counts after policy fallback; three law parents stopped at sequence 76 because the fixture created its foreign recurs_from target after the source, which the SDK correctly refused. All targets are now created before the source, then foreign metadata is made malformed; no cases or sequences are skipped. The ownership module measured 100% in all four dimensions. Completing uncovered legacy/mixed recovery boundaries also exposed two ownership issues: native edits to unrelated edges invalidated the whole prior graph receipt, and SDK preview ordered an existing edge update before its new target creation. Fixes scope invalidation to SDK-replayed changed edge identities and preview creates before updates through one shared SDK wrapper. Legacy fields now use immutable creation origins, preserve native identity/path/original metadata and apply unrelated harness edits; external represented targets join the guarded read set. Preparing focused revert proofs and a replacement CI head."
  "2026-10-26T14:56:11.549Z",codex-agent,"Post-CI fixes and behavioral revert proofs: native relationship invalidation is now scoped to actual SDK-replayed edge identities, not the entire graph. A compensated mixed update/create import preserves its native Task edge AND adds the new represented target. Restoring whole-graph invalidation in an isolated copy fails that SDK read-back regression (0 pass/1 fail). Restoring input-order SDK preview instead of create-before-update fails the same mixed regression before publication (0/1). Restoring blanket legacy edited/path refusal fails native-preserving field locality (0/1). Removing external represented targets from the legacy read set fails the real peer-edit/atomic-refusal regression (0/1, import wrongly succeeds). Every mutant changes only the named behavior, fails behavioral assertions rather than syntax/module loading, and leaves production sources untouched. The original clearing-only identity-law counterexample and all earlier revert proofs remain recorded above."
