  "2026-10-27T09:21:29.966Z",codex-agent,"Installed consumer validation now passes 2/2 (npm and native Bun), including identical-alias origin selection, retained edges and native-field fidelity through JSON and TOON. Projection crash and peer-edit tests pass all 13 SDK projection boundaries on non-git trackers; native peer body C always wins, retries converge without duplicates, foreign package links and native Task references remain untouched. Added parity against the ordinary SDK preview path. Targeted actual CLI tests also expose a refusal mapping gap: ExpectedError previously discarded the MemoryError code/remedy into generic command_failed. The shared command adapter now supplies SDK context.code and context.required for every refusal; actual JSON origin_missing and human output retain --create and leave a same-alias replacement byte-identical through SDK read-back. Focused CLI/native-preview roots pass 3/3. Packed consumers additionally assert this refusal contract."
  "2026-10-27T09:24:18.858Z",codex-agent,"Final adapter revert proofs: forcing direct SDK preview on the installed-code fixture fails 0/1; moving guarded schema hydration outside configuration-only scope fails 0/1; removing only SDK error context.code/context.required fails the typed-refusal regression 0/1. All production mutations restored. These bring semantic behavioral proofs to seventeen, plus the earlier collision-diagnostic reproduction. Combined focused c8 receipts measure portable-preview.ts at 67/67 lines and statements, 3/3 functions, 49/49 branches (100 percent in all four dimensions). Both native SDK and scoped projection paths have the same SDK-read result. Full gate evidence will come from the next pushed head."
  "2026-10-27T09:25:58.402Z",codex-agent,"SDK minimum verification: inspected the published 2026.10.23 declarations and confirmed public runWithConfigurationOnlySettings, resolveTransactionSchema, writeSettings, locateItem and getItemPath are present; the peer minimum remains valid. Main supplies the unchanged development pin 2026.10.24. The new preview adapter has no private SDK import. README documents installed-code exclusion, SDK path-filter/host-bound gaps and structured CLI refusal codes. All review and adapter work is linked to the feature and the existing SDK follow-up, without creating an upstream issue or duplicating the item."
  "2026-10-27T09:39:36.776Z",codex-agent,"The actual host --create remedy passes 1/1 end-to-end: missing origin plus same-alias replacement refuses in JSON and human output without touching the replacement; after the fixture explicitly frees the alias, --create imports a new native id bound to the immutable old origin, and the next ordinary retry reports unchanged. The packed npm/Bun scenarios now assert the same refusal, explicit recreation, full native field/edge read-back and idempotent retry. Typecheck, lint and zero duplication pass after these assertions. Seventeen semantic revert proofs and the diagnostic reproduction are committed in tracker comments; no gate threshold or existing assertion was removed."
  "2026-10-27T09:42:41.125Z",codex-agent,"Completion checkpoint: seventeen semantic revert mutants plus the diagnostic reproduction fail as expected and are restored. Local focused suites pass 21/21 identity/origin/companion, 9/9 validation/corrected receipts, 5/5 final wire validation, 6/6 preview safety/interleavings, 3/3 CLI/native-preview and 1/1 actionable --create tests. Packed installed npm and Bun consumers pass 2/2 before their added explicit-recreation assertions; those assertions are now included in the unchanged CI release gates. Final static checks pass: typecheck, lint, duplication 0 percent across 94 sources, docstrings 38 files / 142 declarations, identity/privacy 0 violations. Source projection coverage is 100/100/100/100. Public read-only validation is rechecking the same source with the merged SDK pin; prior 17-item receipt remains linked. Releasing the claim while final exact-head npm Node 22/26 and Bun Node 26 gates run; feature remains in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-27T11:20:43.635Z",codex-agent,"Resume checkpoint: pushed head 0966f8a is clean and includes origin/main b49840b. CI run 40482997764 Node 26 passed 508/508 tests with zero skips; the unchanged branch gate refused 99.91% (transfer.ts raw-intake validation/recreation branches). Adding focused real-tracker coverage for these paths before the next push. Also checking that foreign creations with copied bookkeeping cannot become compensation authority."
  "2026-10-27T11:24:15.832Z",codex-agent,"Additional ownership reproduction on a real non-git tracker: at intent, a peer creates a Task at the reserved id using the planned source/original bookkeeping but a different body. Before the fix, import throws conflict and compensation deletes the Task (remaining SDK corpus is empty). General rule: matching bookkeeping alone is never proof that this package created a record. Planning and rollback now share ownsCreation: immutable SDK birth type, slug, source, original, origin and represented field fingerprints must agree; fingerprints pass through SDK getItemAt, store decoding and canonical storage normalization. Fixed regression injects Task and Knowledge peer births for raw and policy imports across fresh/recovery read/guard boundaries; retries must preserve them."
  "2026-10-27T11:42:22.923Z",codex-agent,"The new retry regression exposed the second half of copied-bookkeeping authority: after the first refusal preserved a raw Knowledge record, retry incorrectly trusted its mismatched birth body and replaced Peer native body with Owned instructions. The shared legacyBirth check now admits raw-source authority only when the existing parser reproduces represented SDK birth fields (body/title and explicitly carried metadata); native defaults and absent fields remain outside the format ownership. Both import/export admission and birth fallback use it. The parser is moved, unchanged, to portable-source.ts so all paths use one implementation. Added a fixed foreign retry/export case plus must-allow native defaults and CRLF normalization."
  "2026-10-27T11:56:16.730Z",codex-agent,"Two additional behavioral revert proofs passed in isolated non-git source copies; production was unchanged. (18) Restore source/original-only creation ownership in ownsCreation: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"^copied creation bookkeeping\" test/portable-rollback.test.ts fails 0/1 with SDK read-back must retain the foreign creation; the Task was deleted. (19) Restore unfiltered SDK birth authority in legacyBirth: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"^legacy birth authority\" test/portable-validation.test.ts fails 0/1 on the before/after tracker snapshot after importing over the foreign Knowledge body. Both failures are behavioral assertions, with no module/syntax failure. Nineteen semantic mutants plus the earlier diagnostic reproduction are now recorded. Positive boundary/discriminator/raw-birth roots pass 4/4, including all 24 raw/policy, fresh/recovery, intent/read/guard, Task/Knowledge branches. The pinned pm test runner passes 3/3 final raw-birth/native-default/ambiguous-origin/ambiguous-export cases. Every source field authority is conditional on agreement with SDK-normalized birth values; aliases and implicit native defaults are preserved."
  "2026-10-27T12:03:13.883Z",codex-agent,"Final black-box assertions also pass through the pinned pm runner: pm test pm-memory-1363 --run --progress --only-index 19 --shared-host-safe runs all 3 selected roots, including 24 foreign creation/recovery boundaries and the SDK birth discriminator matrix, with zero failures or skips. Final native-default/ambiguous legacy compatibility runner passed 3/3. Focused c8 covers ownsCreation 17/17 statements and 29/29 branches; final legacyBirth 10/10 statements and 7/7 branches. Typecheck, lint, docstrings (39 files/144 declarations), build and pack dry-run (98 files including portable-source) pass; duplication is zero across 95 sources. Main remains b49840b and both changed history streams preserve main as a byte prefix. Nineteen semantic revert proofs are recorded. Clarification: raw admission requires matching SDK-normalized birth bodies, while field authority is limited to represented values that also match; differing native aliases/defaults remain readable. Complete npm Node 22/26 and Bun gates will run on the next pushed head; no new full-gate success is claimed from the superseded 508/508 test run whose coverage gate refused 99.91 percent branches."
  "2026-10-27T12:06:57.066Z",codex-agent,"Pushed executable-code candidate 70b46b7b9a3d84c22ec3e060ebbb21c8d8437919. Exact-candidate CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/actions/runs/40500975059 . Queue receipt: npm Node 22 queued; npm Node 26 queued; Bun Node 26 waits for npm; zero completed full release gates and no final test counts yet. Current PR checks: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/15/checks . The next commit records only this tracker receipt; executable code and tests are unchanged. Local targeted, static, package and revert-proof evidence is in the preceding comments. Queue rules limit post-push waiting to 30 minutes; pending CI is not a pass or an acceptance waiver. Feature stays in_progress and its claim will be released for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-27T12:40:14.344Z",codex-agent,"Final write-set adversary reproduced a remaining creation-ownership gap: a raw foreign Knowledge birth copies the planned body/title/bookkeeping but has a different native description. Import reported imported:1 and cleared Peer native description. Raw receipts correctly exclude implicit field authority for later edits, but that partial receipt cannot prove ownership of a whole creation. ownsCreation now projects EVERY planned core/custom field through the existing metadata writer mapping and compares complete SDK-canonical birth documents before checking portable hashes. This covers omitted legacy defaults and native bookkeeping without reimplementing SDK normalization. Extending the adversary across every planned scalar field before another push."
  "2026-10-27T13:14:58.961Z",codex-agent,"Closing the whole-birth ownership class through the SDK operation identity: verified public CreateCommandOptions.message persists in immutable creation history (1/1 real SDK test). New edge-free creation steps now record their exact per-attempt SDK transaction identity in message; creation proof verifies it, and compensation always uses the same full birth proof even when a message has a transaction prefix. Full-write projection compares every planned core/custom scalar after SDK canonicalDocument normalization, not just the intentionally partial legacy receipt. Additional foreign fixtures cover unplanned registered package metadata, native priority, an unknown schema field and a native Task relationship. Older receipt-less intents derive their field proof through existing SDK birth provenance rather than losing compatibility."
  "2026-10-27T13:39:00.525Z",codex-agent,"The final all-field audit also found hand-written tag CSV in remember(create/update), portable creation and ownershipPatch updates. A real SDK oracle stores one,two as a SINGLE tag when encoded through itemDocumentToMutationOptions; the package split it into one and two. The new black-box codec law failed 0/1 before the fix, and now passes 1/1 across both harnesses, quoted/comma/whitespace/Unicode tags, remember create/update and portable create/update. All four sites now use the public SDK serializer; no manual tag serialization remains. The scalar creation adversary completed 38 peer creations over 19 actual planned scalar fields and both harnesses. Registered/native/custom/relationship foreign birth fixtures use the same SDK operation proof; the custom field fixture is explicitly optional so preflight reaches the competing creation."
  "2026-10-27T13:57:33.393Z",codex-agent,"Final additional semantic revert proofs (20-28), each isolated source mutation and each 0 passed/1 expected failure: omit the SDK-canonical whole-write comparison (foreign description cleared); omit unplanned package-field rejection (foreign native reason deleted); omit SDK create-message verification; omit create-message publication (foreign priority/corpus deleted in both); restore hand-written CSV separately at remember create, remember update, portable create and ownershipPatch update (the SDK tag codec law fails in all four); restore transaction-prefix acceptance before full creation proof in ownsLatest (marked foreign creation deleted). No production file was reverted and no failure was a module/syntax error. Twenty-eight latest-round semantic mutants plus the earlier diagnostic reproduction are recorded, in addition to prior round CAS/window/ownership proofs. Positive evidence: 38 scalar write-set peer creations over 19 planned fields and both harnesses; two older-plan recovery cases and the SDK birth discriminator pass; the final four foreign birth shapes pass after configuring the custom field with supported SDK required/requiredOnCreate/allowUnset options. The tag codec law passes both harnesses and all four writers. Final typecheck, lint, zero duplication across 96 sources, docstrings 39 files/144 declarations, build and 98-file pack dry-run pass. No thresholds or pre-existing assertions were weakened."
